    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick, mini.extra, mini.tabline\n\n### Description\n\nWhen selecting a diagnostic, instead of opening the file (from where the diagnostic originates) in a new tab, it opens the file in the same buffer, which is not consistent with how other pickers work (they open a new tab). \r\n\r\nThis causes problem, as when i need to switch the buffer to look at another open file, i loose the file with the error. \r\n\r\nIs this behaviour expected, or is it a bug?\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.4\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\r\nvim.g.mapleader = ' '\r\nvim.g.maplocalleader = ' '\r\n\r\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath 'data' .. '/lazy/lazy.nvim'\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n  vim.fn.system {\r\n    'git',\r\n    'clone',\r\n    '--filter=blob:none',\r\n    'https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git',\r\n    '--branch=stable', -- latest stable release\r\n    lazypath,\r\n  }\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\n\r\nrequire('lazy').setup({\r\n  'tpope/vim-sleuth',\r\n\r\n  {\r\n    'neovim/nvim-lspconfig',\r\n    dependencies = {\r\n      { 'williamboman/mason.nvim', config = true },\r\n      'williamboman/mason-lspconfig.nvim',\r\n\r\n      { 'j-hui/fidget.nvim',       tag = 'legacy', opts = {} },\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n\r\n  { 'echasnovski/mini.nvim',      version = false },\r\n\r\n  { \"nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons\" },\r\n\r\n  { \"EdenEast/nightfox.nvim\" },\r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\n}, {})\r\n\r\n\r\nlocal servers = {\r\n  rust_analyzer = {},\r\n  hls = {},\r\n  lua_ls = {\r\n    Lua = {\r\n      workspace = { checkThirdParty = false },\r\n      telemetry = { enable = false },\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n\r\nlocal mason_lspconfig = require 'mason-lspconfig'\r\n\r\n\r\nmason_lspconfig.setup {\r\n  ensure_installed = vim.tbl_keys(servers),\r\n}\r\n\r\nmason_lspconfig.setup_handlers {\r\n  function(server_name)\r\n    require('lspconfig')[server_name].setup {\r\n      on_attach =\r\n          function(_, bufnr)\r\n            vim.cmd [[autocmd BufWritePre <buffer> lua vim.lsp.buf.format()]]\r\n          end,\r\n\r\n      settings = servers[server_name],\r\n      filetypes = (servers[server_name] or {}).filetypes,\r\n    }\r\n  end\r\n}\r\nrequire(\"mini.extra\").setup()\r\nrequire('mini.pick').setup({\r\n  options = {\r\n    use_cache = true\r\n  },\r\n  window = {\r\n    config = function()\r\n      height = math.floor(0.618 * vim.o.lines)\r\n      width = math.floor(0.618 * vim.o.columns)\r\n      return {\r\n        anchor = 'NW',\r\n        height = height,\r\n        width = width,\r\n        row = math.floor(0.5 * (vim.o.lines - height)),\r\n        col = math.floor(0.5 * (vim.o.columns - width)),\r\n        border = 'double',\r\n      }\r\n    end,\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/52526849/7dded524-9d98-4c2f-b190-29c8030b85d5\r\n\r\n",
